  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-centered:real-l2-positive-square-order",
    "anchor": "Appendix D.1 bounded selfadjoint spectral calculus and unique nonnegative square root; ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 square-order corollary via Mathlib CFC monotonicity, consumed by B.15",
    "original_text": "Attributed mathematical restatement; exact selected boundary, with internally completed adapters.\nFor any measurable space Ω and any measure μ, let A and B be bounded real linear operators on real L²(μ). If A and B are positive (selfadjoint with nonnegative quadratic form) and B²−A² is positive, then B−A is positive. No finiteness or probability of μ, nontriviality, finite-dimensional L², commutation, or caller CFC instance is assumed. This is an ASTIS auxiliary consequence of positive square-root monotonicity, realized by the canonical complexification of real L²; it is consumed by the actual centered-root result.\nSource anchor: Appendix D.1 bounded selfadjoint spectral calculus and unique nonnegative square root; ASTIS auxiliary real-L2 square-order corollary via Mathlib CFC monotonicity, consumed by B.15",
    "text_sha256": "9ed471114b9b462c10faee2a1369fb98c6cca55fa4051af7bf8576402d52a4e4"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.L2RealSquareOrder.positive_square_order",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/L2RealSquareOrder.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)\n    (A B : Lp ℝ 2 μ →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 μ)\n    (hA : A.IsPositive) (hB : B.IsPositive)\n    (hSquareOrder : (B*B-A*A).IsPositive) :\n    (B-A).IsPositive",
    "statement_sha256": "099c95a5d4d4a160e2c18943755e58e8e89dc87e2dbe95922582504dee961491",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let Omega be any measurable space, mu any measure on Omega, and H=Lp(R,2,mu), the complete real Hilbert space of square-integrable measurable functions modulo mu-almost-everywhere equality. Let A,B:H->H be bounded real-linear operators. Assume A and B are positive, meaning symmetric/selfadjoint with nonnegative real quadratic form, and assume B composed with B minus A composed with A is positive. Then B-A is positive: it is symmetric/selfadjoint and <f,(B-A)f> >= 0 for every f in H. All data are universally quantified. No commutation, finite measure, probability, finite dimension or nontriviality assumption is made. The zero Hilbert space and admissible zero operators are included. Products are composition of endomorphisms of the same real Hilbert space. No functional-calculus witness or further hypothesis is supplied by the caller.",
    "text_sha256": "0a2b821fd6f95296e6ede60fe0d2cc2213e89cdf4e52fd8a49baee78756dae2d",
    "decoder": "/root/anonymous_decoder64",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "bd0c01074ff9ae634b300ec43993943358d82d1b75fea6916484fabaa1c2bdef",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "dfa4906527c35c1684d8ce626c56cbcc41985f2bfb517f65d17c5cba1dd3f2ad",
    "source_text_visible": false
  },
