  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let Omega be any measurable space, mu any measure on Omega, and H=Lp(R,2,mu), the complete real Hilbert space of square-integrable measurable functions modulo mu-almost-everywhere equality. Let A,B:H->H be bounded real-linear operators. Assume A and B are positive, meaning symmetric/selfadjoint with nonnegative real quadratic form, and assume B composed with B minus A composed with A is positive. Then B-A is positive: it is symmetric/selfadjoint and <f,(B-A)f> >= 0 for every f in H. All data are universally quantified. No commutation, finite measure, probability, finite dimension or nontriviality assumption is made. The zero Hilbert space and admissible zero operators are included. Products are composition of endomorphisms of the same real Hilbert space. No functional-calculus witness or further hypothesis is supplied by the caller.",
    "text_sha256": "0a2b821fd6f95296e6ede60fe0d2cc2213e89cdf4e52fd8a49baee78756dae2d",
